IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lrnt-dates`
IMPORT `lrnt-claims`

-- Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1956 (NT), Parts IV to X -- worked cases for the claims questions.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`27 Jun 1956` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 6 1956
`28 Jun 1956` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 6 1956
`31 Dec 1991` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 12 1991
`1 Jan 1992` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 1992
`1 Jan 2000` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2000
`31 Jul 2001` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 7 2001
`1 Aug 2001` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 8 2001
`1 Jan 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2020
`1 Jun 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2020

`ONE ACTION` MEANS `s 12(3)(b) does not apply: only one action has been brought for the damage (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`FIRST JUDGMENT HERE` MEANS `s 12(3)(b) does not limit your costs: judgment was first given in this action`
`MAY GET COSTS` MEANS `you may get costs: the court is of opinion there was reasonable ground for bringing this action (s 12(3)(b))`
`NO COSTS` MEANS `no costs: this is not the action in which judgment was first given, and the court is not of opinion there was reasonable ground for bringing it (s 12(3)(b), the text's no)`

`ME` MEANS `I suffered the damage myself`
`DEPENDANT` MEANS `I am a dependant claiming under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 for the death of a person who was partly at fault`
`THIRD PERSON` MEANS `I suffered damage because of the injured person's damage (for example loss of their society or services)`
`NEGLIGENCE` MEANS `negligence (a tort of negligence)`
`CONCURRENT CONTRACT` MEANS `a breach of a contractual duty of care that runs alongside a duty of care in tort`
`STATUTORY DUTY` MEANS `a breach of statutory duty`
`NOT A WRONG` MEANS `something else (for example an intentional tort, or a breach of contract with no duty of care in tort)`

`APPORTIONED` MEANS `yes: your claim is not defeated by your own share of fault, but your damages are reduced as the court thinks just and equitable (s 16(1))`
`NAVIGATION ACT` MEANS `no: s 16 does not apply to a claim under s 259 of the Navigation Act 1912 (Cth) (s 21(a), the text's no)`
`WRONG BEFORE 1956` MEANS `no: s 16 does not apply where the wrong occurred before 28 June 1956 (s 21(b), the text's no)`
`EARLIER S 16` MEANS `the earlier s 16 applies: the wrong was before 1 August 2001 and proceedings were commenced, or a settlement agreed, before that day (s 21A(3)); that earlier text is not encoded here (NOTHING-kind)`
`S 16 IF FAILS` MEANS `s 16 does not apply: the damage was not partly the result of your own failure to take reasonable care and partly of another person's wrong (negligence, a concurrent contractual duty of care, or breach of statutory duty) (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`CONTRACT DEFENCE` MEANS `s 16 does not save the claim from a defence arising under a contract (s 16(2), the text's no)`

`EMPLOYER LIABLE` MEANS `yes: your employer is liable as if you and the fellow worker were not in common employment (s 22(1)); the "common employment" defence is gone`
`S 22 NOT ARISE` MEANS `s 22 does not arise: the injury was not caused by the wrongful act, neglect or default of a fellow worker of the same employer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S 22 BEFORE 1956` MEANS `s 22 does not reach it: the wrongful act was before 28 June 1956 (s 22(2), NOTHING-kind)`

`EMPLOYER INDEMNIFIES` MEANS `you need not indemnify your employer, and your employer must indemnify you for your liability (s 22A(1)(a), (b))`
`OTHERWISE INDEMNIFIED` MEANS `you need not indemnify your employer (s 22A(1)(a)); your employer need not indemnify you, because you are otherwise entitled to indemnity (s 22A(1)(b)); your employer takes over your rights under that insurance or indemnity (s 22A(2))`
`MISCONDUCT` MEANS `s 22A(1) does not apply: serious and wilful, or gross, misconduct (s 22A(3), the text's no); the general law decides`
`NOT VICARIOUS` MEANS `s 22A does not arise: your employer is not vicariously liable for the tort (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

`PARENT` MEANS `I am their parent (father, mother, grandparent, step-parent, or I stand in the place of a parent to them)`
`SPOUSE` MEANS `I am their spouse or de facto partner`
`CHILD` MEANS `I am their child (son, daughter, grandchild, stepchild, or they stand in the place of a parent to me)`
`SIBLING` MEANS `I am their sibling or half-sibling`
`NO RELATION` MEANS `none of these`
`SHOCK PARENT OR SPOUSE` MEANS `yes: the wrongdoer's liability extends to your nervous shock as a parent, spouse or de facto partner, whether or not you saw or heard it (s 25(1)(a)); the action must be brought in the Supreme Court (s 25(5))`
`SHOCK FAMILY SAW` MEANS `yes: the wrongdoer's liability extends to your nervous shock as a member of the family who saw or heard it (s 25(1)(b)); the action must be brought in the Supreme Court (s 25(5))`
`SHOCK NOT SEEN` MEANS `no, not under s 25(1)(b): it did not happen within your sight or hearing (the text's no: its "where" fails); a claim under the general law, which s 24 keeps open, is not decided here`
`SHOCK NOT FAMILY` MEANS `s 25 does not extend liability to you: you are not a member of the family within s 23 (NOTHING-kind); a claim under the general law, which s 24 keeps open, is not decided here`
`SHOCK NO ONE` MEANS `s 25 does not arise: no one was killed, injured or put in peril by the act, neglect or default (NOTHING-kind)`
`SHOCK BEFORE 1956` MEANS `s 25 does not reach it: the injury was caused before 28 June 1956 (NOTHING-kind)`

`WITHOUT LEAVE` MEANS `yes, without leave: the insured company was being wound up (s 26(2), s 27(1), (3))`
`WITH LEAVE` MEANS `yes, with the court's leave, which the court may grant (s 27(1), (3)); a judgment already obtained against the wrongdoer is no bar (s 27(4))`
`LEAVE REFUSED` MEANS `no: leave must be refused, because the court is satisfied the insurer may disclaim liability under the policy and the proceedings to establish that have been taken (s 27(3), the text's no)`
`NO INSURANCE` MEANS `Part VIII does not arise: the wrongdoer had no insurance against this liability (the text's no: the "if" of s 26(1) fails)`

`TERRITORY LIABLE` MEANS `the Territory, jointly and severally with the detainee, up to $5,000 (s 29A(3), (4))`
`PARENT LIABLE` MEANS `the parent, jointly and severally with the child, up to $5,000 from the parents together (s 29A(2), (4))`
`NO PARENT` MEANS `no parent is liable under s 29A: the child was not living with that parent, or was in full time employment (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`NO ONE ELSE` MEANS `no one else is liable under s 29A: the person was not under 18, or the damage was not intentional, or it was caused before 1 January 1992 (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

`S 34(1)` MEANS `not liable: you destroyed the dog under a law of the Territory, or because it was so diseased or injured that it was humane (s 34(1))`
`S 34(2)` MEANS `not liable: you destroyed the dog at the request of someone you had reasonable cause to believe was its owner (s 34(2))`
`S 33(1)` MEANS `a defence: you were not trespassing, there was an attack (or reasonable belief in one about to happen) on you, another person or an animal or bird of yours, and you did not provoke it (s 33(1))`
`PRIMA FACIE` MEANS `a prima facie defence: you were the occupier of the premises, or there with the occupier's authority (s 33(3)); it can be displaced by showing that the s 33(1) conditions were not met`
`NO DOG DEFENCE` MEANS `these sections give no defence on these facts (s 33, s 34, the text's no); a defence under the general law is not decided here`

`CANNOT REFUSE` MEANS `no: you are entitled to take the dog in, and refusing you entry, accommodation or service only because of the dog is an offence (maximum 4 penalty units) by the occupier or person in charge (s 35)`
`NOT ONLY THE DOG` MEANS `s 35 does not decide it: the refusal was not only because of the dog (NOTHING-kind)`
`S 35 NOT REACH` MEANS `s 35 does not reach it: it covers a wholly or partially blind or deaf person with a guide dog or hearing dog, in a public building or place or a passenger vehicle, vessel or craft for hire or reward (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 12(3) -- several actions for the same damage`

-- One action only.
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(a) -- the most I can recover in total from several actions` 80000 0 EQUALS 80000
-- First judgment 100,000; later judgments 30,000: capped at 100,000.
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(a) -- the most I can recover in total from several actions` 100000 30000 EQUALS 100000
-- A first judgment of nothing caps everything at nothing.
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(a) -- the most I can recover in total from several actions` 0 50000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(b) -- do I get my costs in this action` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ONE ACTION`
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(b) -- do I get my costs in this action` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `FIRST JUDGMENT HERE`
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(b) -- do I get my costs in this action` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `MAY GET COSTS`
#ASSERT `s 12(3)(b) -- do I get my costs in this action` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO COSTS`

§ `Part V -- does apportionment apply`

-- Arguments: who, own failure, the act, wrong on, Navigation Act claim, begun before 1 August 2001, contract defence.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NAVIGATION ACT`
-- The day before, and the day of, 28 June 1956 (edges).
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `27 Jun 1956` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `WRONG BEFORE 1956`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `28 Jun 1956` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
-- s 21A: a wrong on 31 July 2001 with proceedings already begun; on 1 August 2001; on 31 July 2001 with nothing begun.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `31 Jul 2001` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EARLIER S 16`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Aug 2001` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `31 Jul 2001` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
-- No fault of the claimant's own; an intentional tort.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` FALSE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S 16 IF FAILS`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NOT A WRONG` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S 16 IF FAILS`
-- The other two kinds of wrong.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `STATUTORY DUTY` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `CONCURRENT CONTRACT` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `CONTRACT DEFENCE`
-- A dependant (s 17(2)) and a third person (s 18).
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `DEPENDANT` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- does apportionment for contributory negligence apply to my claim` `THIRD PERSON` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPORTIONED`

§ `Part V -- how much after the reduction`

-- 200,000 reduced by 25%: 150,000.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 25 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 150000
-- A limit of 100,000 applies: 100,000 (s 16(4)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 25 TRUE 100000 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- The limit equal to the reduced amount, and 1 below it (edges).
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 25 TRUE 150000 EQUALS JUST 150000
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 25 TRUE 149999 EQUALS JUST 149999
-- No reduction, and a 100% reduction.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- 100,000 reduced by 33%: 67,000.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `DEPENDANT` TRUE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 100000 33 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 67000
-- s 16 does not apply: no amount.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- how much can I recover after the reduction` `ME` FALSE `NEGLIGENCE` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 25 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part VI -- common employment`

#ASSERT `s 22 -- can I hold my employer liable for a fellow worker's wrong` TRUE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `EMPLOYER LIABLE`
#ASSERT `s 22 -- can I hold my employer liable for a fellow worker's wrong` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `S 22 NOT ARISE`
#ASSERT `s 22 -- can I hold my employer liable for a fellow worker's wrong` TRUE `27 Jun 1956` EQUALS `S 22 BEFORE 1956`
#ASSERT `s 22 -- can I hold my employer liable for a fellow worker's wrong` TRUE `28 Jun 1956` EQUALS `EMPLOYER LIABLE`
#ASSERT `s 22A -- who bears the liability for my tort at work` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT VICARIOUS`
#ASSERT `s 22A -- who bears the liability for my tort at work` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MISCONDUCT`
#ASSERT `s 22A -- who bears the liability for my tort at work` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `MISCONDUCT`
#ASSERT `s 22A -- who bears the liability for my tort at work` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `OTHERWISE INDEMNIFIED`
#ASSERT `s 22A -- who bears the liability for my tort at work` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `EMPLOYER INDEMNIFIES`

§ `Part VII -- nervous shock`

#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `PARENT` FALSE EQUALS `SHOCK PARENT OR SPOUSE`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `SPOUSE` FALSE EQUALS `SHOCK PARENT OR SPOUSE`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `CHILD` TRUE EQUALS `SHOCK FAMILY SAW`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `CHILD` FALSE EQUALS `SHOCK NOT SEEN`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `SIBLING` TRUE EQUALS `SHOCK FAMILY SAW`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `SIBLING` FALSE EQUALS `SHOCK NOT SEEN`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `NO RELATION` TRUE EQUALS `SHOCK NOT FAMILY`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `PARENT` TRUE EQUALS `SHOCK NO ONE`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `27 Jun 1956` TRUE `PARENT` TRUE EQUALS `SHOCK BEFORE 1956`
#ASSERT `s 25 -- can I claim for nervous shock as a family member` `28 Jun 1956` TRUE `PARENT` TRUE EQUALS `SHOCK PARENT OR SPOUSE`

§ `Part VIII -- the insurer`

#ASSERT `s 27 -- can I sue the wrongdoer's insurer directly` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO INSURANCE`
-- Winding up: no leave needed, so the leave bar does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 27 -- can I sue the wrongdoer's insurer directly` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `WITHOUT LEAVE`
#ASSERT `s 27 -- can I sue the wrongdoer's insurer directly` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `LEAVE REFUSED`
#ASSERT `s 27 -- can I sue the wrongdoer's insurer directly` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `WITH LEAVE`
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I can recover from the insurer` 100000 250000 0 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I can recover from the insurer` 100000 250000 200000 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I can recover from the insurer` 100000 250000 300000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I can recover from the insurer` 100000 100000 0 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I can recover from the insurer` 100001 100000 0 EQUALS 100000

§ `Part VIIIA -- damage to property by children`

-- Arguments: damaged on, under 18, intentional, a detainee, lives with the parent, full time employed.
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `PARENT LIABLE`
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO PARENT`
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO PARENT`
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO ONE ELSE`
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO ONE ELSE`
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TERRITORY LIABLE`
-- A detainee who lives with a parent: the Territory, not the parent (s 29A(5)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `TERRITORY LIABLE`
-- The day before, and the day of, commencement (edges).
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `31 Dec 1991` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO ONE ELSE`
#ASSERT `s 29A -- who else is liable for the damage a child caused my property` `1 Jan 1992` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `PARENT LIABLE`
-- The cap of $5,000: below, at, just over.
#ASSERT `s 29A -- the most I can recover from the parents or the Territory` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 3000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `s 29A -- the most I can recover from the parents or the Territory` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 29A -- the most I can recover from the parents or the Territory` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5001 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 29A -- the most I can recover from the parents or the Territory` `1 Jun 2020` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 12000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 29A -- the most I can recover from the parents or the Territory` `1 Jun 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3000 EQUALS 0

§ `Part X -- dogs`

#ASSERT `s 32 -- is the dog's owner liable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32 -- is the dog's owner liable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 32 -- is the dog's owner liable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: destroyed, under a law or humane, at the apparent owner's request, not a trespasser, occupier or authorised,
-- attack, provoked.
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S 34(1)`
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S 34(2)`
-- Only injured, so s 34 cannot help even if humane; attack, not trespassing, not provoked.
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `S 33(1)`
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO DOG DEFENCE`
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO DOG DEFENCE`
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `PRIMA FACIE`
#ASSERT `s 33 and s 34 -- do I have a defence for killing or injuring a dog` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `PRIMA FACIE`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can I be refused entry with my guide dog or hearing dog` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CANNOT REFUSE`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can I be refused entry with my guide dog or hearing dog` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ONLY THE DOG`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can I be refused entry with my guide dog or hearing dog` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S 35 NOT REACH`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can I be refused entry with my guide dog or hearing dog` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `S 35 NOT REACH`
